==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{m|enm|*clumpe}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{m|ang|clymppe}}, a variant of {{m|ang|clympre||a lump or mass of metal}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*klumpô||mass, lump, clump; clasp}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*glembʰ-||lump, clamp}}.
Alternatively, possibly from {{etyl|dum|en}} {{m|dum|clompe}} or {{etyl|gml|en}} {{m|gml|klumpe}}<ref>[http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/clump%5B1%5D clump] in Merriam-Webster's dictionary</ref> (compare German {{m|de|Klumpen}}). Cognates include Danish {{m|da|klump}} (probably from Low German as well<ref>{{R:ODS online|klump}}</ref>). Compare Norwegian (bokmål) {{m|no|klump}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/klʌmp/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|en-us-clump.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ʌmp|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[cluster]] or [[lump]]; an unshaped piece or mass.
# A [[thick]] [[group]] or [[bunch]], especially of [[bush]]es or hair.
#* Hawthorne
#*: a '''clump''' of shrubby trees
# A [[dull]] [[thud]].
# The [[compressed]] [[clay]] of [[coal]] [[strata]].
#: {{rfquotek|Brande & C}}
# A small group of trees or plants.

